      "content": "Recognizing the evolving dialogue around our collections, this policy balances the urgent commitment to repatriating disputed artifacts with the longstanding principle that certain cultural treasures belong to humanity as a whole. By integrating perspectives on universal heritage, we aim to create a nuanced framework that supports ethical restitution while ensuring the safety, accessibility, and scholarly value of items that will continue to inspire global understanding. This approach seeks to honor historical justice without diminishing the museum's critical role as a steward of shared human knowledge.\n</think>\n\nThis policy reflects the museum's commitment to balancing ethical restitution with the principle that universal heritage belongs to all humanity. By acknowledging the importance of some items remaining in our care for global access, we aim to foster an inclusive dialogue that respects historical justice while preserving our role as a steward of shared human knowledge. Ultimately, this framework seeks to honor past wrongs and protect the future access to these culturally significant treasures.",
